'''March 7, 14, & 21... 10:00am -- 12:30pm'''

If you have an old Windows 10 machine you can't upgrade, but need to get more life out of...

If you want a computer that respects your privacy...

If you want to truly control your technology...

If you want to learn more about computers, or specifically Linux...

Join us for three Saturdays of learning Linux and other open source software. This workshop is not focused on the needs of technologists, but on everyday computer users. We'll take you from the install through basic computer skills, productivity and customizing your system, with plenty of help and hand-holding along the way.

The workshop will be led by Susan Sons, a geek with over 30 years of Linux experience, and a cast of helpers.

